<rst>
    <header>
        <relations>
            <rel name="concession" type="rst"/>
            <rel name="elaboration" type="rst"/>
            <rel name="justify" type="rst"/>
            <rel name="sequence" type="multinuc"/>
        </relations>
    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="9" relname="justify">I've seen many times over the years in software development</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="9" relname="sequence">where the developer(s)believes the application is intuitive to them</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="9" relname="sequence">and when the end-user finally sees the finished product,</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="9" relname="sequence">the end-user does not even know where to begin to use the interface.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="8" relname="span">With this being said, isn't the "intuitiveness" of the UI, really a subjective analysis?</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="5" relname="elaboration">Where as, being intuitive to one user may be perceived as very confusing to another.....</segment>
        <group id="7" type="span"/>
        <group id="8" type="span" parent="7" relname="span"/>
        <group id="9" type="multinuc" parent="10" relname="span"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="8" relname="concession"/>
    </body>
</rst>
